  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, and for PCA the same comparison showed avgpool (0.591) clearly outperforming transformer (0.519). However, we have only one data point on aggregation for scvi_n200. Question: Does the avgpool > transformer finding for PCA generalize to the scvi_n200 encoder, or might transformer aggregation extract more from scvi's learned latent representations? This experiment isolates exactly one variable (aggregation: avgpool → transformer) against the current best configuration, making it a clean 1-factor comparison. Why best next step: It is the most direct logical extension of the strongest result, it is low-risk (builds on proven components), and the outcome will either confirm we can rule out transformer aggregation across encoders or reveal a surprising interaction that would redirect the search. Under a limited budget, confirming or refuting this aggregation choice before investing in more complex multimodal or new-encoder experiments is the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
